/*
 * Important equations:
 * Omega = number of particles / (number of particles in box 1! * number of particles in box 2!...)
 * S = Boltzmann constant * ln(omega)
 * 
 * The plan:
 * Set up the entropy of a given system. Move 1 random particle to a neighboring box. Check if the delta entropy is greater than -0.6 or like -0.7, basically allow some decrease because entropy is like that and tends to sometimes be random (to reach the highest highs you much first go down to the lows). If yes, make it the new norm. If no, select another particle
 */


